steps.text:
Below is a minimal, self‑contained **React Todo List** component that lets you:

* **Add** new tasks  
* **Mark** tasks as complete/incomplete (toggle)  
* **Delete** tasks  

It uses only React’s built‑in hooks (`useState`) and plain HTML elements, so you can drop it into any existing React project (e.g., a Create‑React‑App app) without additional dependencies.

---

### `TodoList.jsx`

```jsx
import React, { useState } from "react";

/**
 * Simple Todo List component
 *
 * Features:
 *   • Add a new todo
 *   • Toggle complete / incomplete
 *   • Delete a todo
 *
 * Usage:
 *   <TodoList />
 */
export default function TodoList() {
  // Each todo: { id: number, text: string, completed: boolean }
  const [todos, setTodos] = useState([]);
  const [newText, setNewText] = useState("");

  // Generate a simple incremental id (good enough for a demo)
  const nextId = React.useRef(1);

  /** Add a new todo */
  const handleAdd = (e) => {
    e.preventDefault();
    const trimmed = newText.trim();
    if (!trimmed) return; // ignore empty entries

    const todo = {
      id: nextId.current++,
      text: trimmed,
      completed: false,
    };
    setTodos((prev) => [...prev, todo]);
    setNewText("");
  };

  /** Toggle complete flag */
  const toggleComplete = (id) => {
    setTodos((prev) =>
      prev.map((t) =>
        t.id === id ? { ...t, completed: !t.completed } : t
      )
    );
  };

  /** Delete a todo */
  const deleteTodo = (id) => {
    setTodos((prev) => prev.filter((t) => t.id !== id));
  };

  return (
    <div style={styles.container}>
      <h2>Todo List</h2>

      {/* Add new todo */}
      <form onSubmit={handleAdd} style={styles.form}>
        <input
          type="text"
          placeholder="What needs to be done?"
          value={newText}
          onChange={(e) => setNewText(e.target.value)}
          style={styles.input}
        />
        <button type="submit" style={styles.addButton}>
          Add
        </button>
      </form>

      {/* List of todos */}
      <ul style={styles.list}>
        {todos.map((todo) => (
          <li key={todo.id} style={styles.listItem}>
            <input
              type="checkbox"
              checked={todo.completed}
              onChange={() => toggleComplete(todo.id)}
            />
            <span
              style={{{{
                ...styles.text,
                textDecoration: todo.completed ? "line-through" : "none",
                color: todo.completed ? "#888" : "#000",
              }}
            >
              {todo.text}
            </span>
            <button
              onClick={() => deleteTodo(todo.id)}
              style={styles.deleteButton}
            >
              ✕
            </button>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>

      {todos.length === 0 && <p style={styles.empty}>No tasks yet!</p>}
    </div>
  );
}

/* Simple inline styles – feel free to replace with CSS classes */
const styles = {
  container: {
    maxWidth: "400px",
    margin: "0 auto",
    padding: "1rem",
    border: "1px solid #ddd",
    borderRadius: "8px",
    fontFamily: "Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif",
  },
  form: {
    display: "flex",
    marginBottom: "1rem",
  },
  input: {
    flexGrow: 1,
    padding: "0.5rem",
    fontSize: "1rem",
  },
  addButton: {
    marginLeft: "0.5rem",
    padding: "0.5rem 1rem",
    fontSize: "1rem",
    cursor: "pointer",
  },
  list: {
    listStyle: "none",
    padding: 0,
  },
  listItem: {
    display: "flex",
    alignItems: "center",
    marginBottom: "0.5rem",
  },
  text: {
    flexGrow: 1,
    marginLeft: "0.5rem",
  },
  deleteButton: {
    marginLeft: "0.5rem",
    background: "transparent",
    border: "none",
    color: "#c00",
    cursor: "pointer",
    fontSize: "1.2rem",
  },
  empty: {
    textAlign: "center",
    color: "#666",
    fontStyle: "italic",
  },
};
```

---

### How to use it

1. **Save** the file (e.g., `TodoList.jsx`) inside your React project’s component folder.  
2. **Import** and render it where you need the todo list:

   ```jsx
   import React from "react";
   import TodoList from "./TodoList";

   function App() {
     return (
       <div>
         <h1>My App</h1>
         <TodoList />
       </div>
     );
   }

   export default App;
   ```

3. Run your app (`npm start` / `yarn start`). You’ll see a small todo list with an input box, an **Add** button, and a list that lets you tick items as completed or delete them.

Feel free to adapt the styling, add persistence (e.g., `localStorage` or a backend), or extend the functionality (editing items, filtering, etc.). The core logic is intentionally kept straightforward for easy understanding and quick customization.
